\summary{Diploma and coursework of KPI (Kyiv) per the Ukrainian standard DSTU 3008:2015}
\begin{description}
A LaTeX class for the bachelor diploma project and courseworks of Igor Sikorsky Kyiv
Polytechnic Institute, Faculty of Informatics and Computer Engineering, typeset per the
Ukrainian standard DSTU 3008:2015 and the department guide. It covers the whole diploma
package: title page, assignment, Ukrainian and English abstracts with counted pages,
figures, tables, sources and appendices, the project sheet and A3 drawing sheets with ESKD
title blocks, and tables continued across pages.

The class needs LuaLaTeX. It uses Times New Roman and Courier New, required by the guide,
and falls back to TeX Gyre Termes and Cursor where they are missing. The documentation is
in Ukrainian.
\end{description}
\begin{announcement}
kpi-thesis is a LaTeX class for the bachelor diploma project and courseworks of Igor Sikorsky
Kyiv Polytechnic Institute, typeset per the Ukrainian standard DSTU 3008:2015: title pages,
assignment, abstracts with counted totals, project sheet and A3 drawing sheets with ESKD
title blocks, and tables continued across pages. Templates, a normcontrol linter and a
Claude Code plugin are in the repository.
\end{announcement}
\begin{note}
First upload. Times New Roman is what the university guide requires, but the class does not
depend on it: without it the class uses TeX Gyre Termes and Cursor.
\end{note}
\file{../kpi-thesis.zip}
